Benny is a human child of nine in [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]], serious beyond his years and hard to one-up. He carries a heavy pick he calls an exemplar weapon, an aspect of himself, and has since added a falcata and a chainsword. He picks the Party's locks, drives its car and keeps its money. He wears a sailcloth sports poncho made for him by [[Org/Garrick Textiles/index|Garrick Textiles]], and answers to false names such as Bennix Plasmadio when the Party needs them.

His father reaches him in his sleep across a black void and shows himself as a shifting shape of light circled by three turning rings. Benny reports to him, and the two also trade faxes. His father passes on what [[Belvedere]] learns, and set Benny to find a twelve-sided green stone, ringing with the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], that was stolen from a Belvedere archive.

He was killed in the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]] and came back, and now bears [[Aut]]'s hidden mark. The piece of himself he left behind in the [[Pharos]] was later called back into him. He helped kill the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] to honor [[People/Argyle|Argyle]].

He keeps company with [[People/Johnny|Johnny Skyfall]], [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]]. Over the Party's six months of downtime he worked as a security advisor to the guards of the [[Geography/Calaria/Eilebrin Observatory|Eilebrin Observatory]].
